From f7e3df030259b4fe646b325523a474e02a2868c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LibreELEC Hades <dev@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:26:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the cover of the level 5 block by the edges of what
 is drawn over the picture

A frame with something drawn over its picture no longer takes the level
5 offsets of every bar out: the packer is told, per edge, which edges
what is drawn over the picture reaches. Two sources know where it went:
the occupancy rectangles of the GUI (the pass of the packer, or the mask
of the GUI texture, asked for at the fold), and the rectangle of the PQ
subtitles drawn into the picture, which the overlay renderer now gives
back. An edge that nothing reaches keeps its offsets, so a bar that no
subtitle covers stays gated and the black floor of a display with local
dimming stays down. Any doubt keeps every edge taken, as before.
